# Generated by tools/ci/costs.c; don't edit it by hand (docs/commands/ci.md, "Shard costs").
# What each command of tools/ci/correctness.tests costs a runner of the hosted row native-none-O3, for `parallel --shard
# K/N --costs` (docs/commands/parallel.md): its time times the CPUs it held (its heading's, at most the runner's), in
# seconds, then its title as its heading has it. `costs collect` makes it from the row's job logs, at the revisions
# below (`revision`, with its jobs): a command's cost is the 90th percentile (nearest rank) of its samples, each
# scaled to the slowest CPU's time by the speeds of the CPUs the jobs drew (`cpu`: its jobs, its time against the
# slowest's over the commands both ran, `-` where too few, and its model). Where every sample failed, its longest
# failure, a lower bound (`lower-bound`); where it has none, the row's median per CPU times its CPUs (`unmeasured`),
# which `costs refresh` also gives a command the inventory adds. The costs only deal the commands to the shards: a
# stale cost makes a shard longer, never a test go missing.
